      "correspondence": "The number of left cosets of VD in KD is bounded by [K:K∩W]≤b. Choose a representative r of each left coset of VD in G. Any other prolongation is gA with g=rvd, yielding gA=(rvr⁻¹)(rA). The subgroup at each finite layer contains V, so its orbit partition is coarser.",
