    "TIC constructs the common tame lift and explains why characters with ℓ-primary targets kill wild inertia at p≠ℓ. Galois transitivity on prolongations and the initial uniform abelian class-rank estimate are cited inputs. QCS explains the obstruction bit, its encoding by the sign character and the square-zero endomorphism giving each subsequent squaring step."
